<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ravano dalle Carceri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1216">1216</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ravano dalle Carceri was a nobleman from Verona who took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a> and became lord of the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a>, or Negroponte, around 1205. He made himself a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1209, granting it trading privileges, and after his death in 1216 his lands were divided among his heirs, giving rise to the three lordships known as the Triarchy of Negroponte.</p></div>
